<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fubing system</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as fubing</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The fubing system was a militia system used in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-wei">Western Wei</a> to the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a>, in which farming households provided soldiers in return for land. It supplied troops cheaply, but as frontier wars demanded permanent professional armies it broke down in the eighth century and was replaced by standing forces under military governors.</p></div>
